.TH UCABLE-AGENT-HELPER 1 "2026-10-13" "ucabled" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ucable\-agent\-helper \- QR code window for ucabled
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ucable\-agent\-helper
.RB [ \-\-rp " RP" ]
.RB [ \-\-layer\-shell ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout " SECS" ]
.RB [ \-\-request\-type " mc|ga" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The helper is spawned by
.BR ucable\-agent (1)
for a single prompt and exits when that interaction ends.
It is not usually run by hand; any UI can replace it as long as it follows
the contract in
.IR docs/helper-contract.md .
.PP
It reads the caBLE URL from the first line of standard input and renders it
as a QR code; a later
.B found
line blurs the code and asks the user to confirm on the phone.
.PP
The URL is a per-transaction secret, so it only ever travels over standard
input.  Everything on the command line is display-only and world-readable
via /proc; unknown arguments, including any FIDO:/ URL, are ignored.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-rp " RP"
Show the relying party
.I RP
above the QR code.  Display-only.
.TP
.B \-\-layer\-shell
Draw as a Wayland layer\-shell surface instead of a window.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECS"
Close the window after
.I SECS
seconds.  Default 300.
.TP
.BI \-\-request\-type " mc|ga"
Phrase the caption for
.B mc
(authenticatorMakeCredential) or
.B ga
(authenticatorGetAssertion).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B UCABLED_HELPER_LAYER_SHELL
Truthy to imply
.BR \-\-layer\-shell .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; non\-zero on cancel, close, timeout or signal.  The daemon
treats any exit as "the user gave up on the phone".
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ucabled (1),
.BR ucable\-agent (1)
